d a basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(G).$" :question/worked-solution "In order to find a basis of $\\text{Col}(G),$ we reduce the matrix $G$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 2 & -\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}^{′} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, only the $1$st column is a pivot column, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one. \n\nThe $1$st column from the original matrix is ${g}_{1}.$ So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(G)$ is ${{g}_{1}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-34513/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39d79985-57fa-554a-b697-4bd6dd71cbe2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-34513"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75946/selection/67c54c6b184890511e60fe85a593aff8e0c290181c4eb7a5b20a0af6697927bf" :answer/id #uuid "1aad852c-2e2e-5147-85a0-fe54a6ecea3f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{{}{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\text{}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(P)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75946/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "50c2dbe5-865b-5917-9523-96b91d2f1520" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75946/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "88021d76-c1f0-5637-9102-dfe97a03afdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75946/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "bd4a9bb1-77ec-5aa9-89dc-c87737fa65f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75946/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "fe53993f-4b0f-53ca-b955-ebf036acb740" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75946/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c59fa0ab-ce77-575f-ad45-7ebfafaf8d75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75946/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-75946/selection/67c54c6b184890511e60fe85a593aff8e0c290181c4eb7a5b20a0af6697927bf" "q-75946/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-75946/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-75946/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-75946/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75946" :question/id #uuid "0d789983-1102-5910-a9c9-78cf71dfe4bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-75946" :question/problem "The matrix $P$ is given below. Let ${p}_{1}$, ${p}_{2}$, and ${p}_{3}$ be the respective columns of $P.$\nDetermine if $B=\\text{{}{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(P).$ \nIf that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${p}_{3}={x}_{1}{p}_{1}+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}.$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $P$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(P)$ is ${{p}_{1},{p}_{2}},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nNow, since the $3$rd column of the reduced matrix is a non-pivot column, then the entries in that column tell us the coefficients needed to express ${p}_{3}$ as a linear combination of all the other columns in the original matrix. So, we have\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{p}_{3}}={{(-2)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{p}_{1}}+{{(1)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{p}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=(-2)\\cdot 1=-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-75946/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db27967e-f80c-587b-9b10-28f1a5518f57"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75946"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-111508/selection/fe181dcbae0b8d386329d4879f2be581227c0752e0dd0ae17c83b6106a54d21e" :answer/id #uuid "54ebbf84-1837-5a39-af8d-a94ee5670110" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{{}{t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\text{}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(T)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111508/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "899ea90a-a0e1-5684-9ce1-b562f5248656" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111508/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "0897d960-be28-5a88-bd28-f5a1ecaf8dbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure 