, a basis of $\\text{Col}(T)$ is ${{t}_{1},{t}_{2}}.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $\\text{{}{t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\text{}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(T).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-111503/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db27967e-f80c-587b-9b10-28f1a5518f57"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-111503"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75977/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "9a481670-87aa-5d73-b55b-24ac0bcf5cea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75977/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "d7207f1f-daa5-5147-87d3-eb472d6f6309" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75977/selection/38861295b3aa8ed9988b03b0db770a1218cf647dc8d71f5fd60d72459c23a902" :answer/id #uuid "31b5e244-83a3-5d12-afc8-a9372b8df88f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${{h}_{1},{h}_{2}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(H)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75977/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "6cacfe11-ab54-5bb3-a71b-702cef14cc1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75977/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "eea48f90-7c93-5265-bc16-813d42c5b025" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75977/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8cb9362b-9d8a-56fa-9b90-b9937c0b4e53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75977/selection/38861295b3aa8ed9988b03b0db770a1218cf647dc8d71f5fd60d72459c23a902" :answer-field/choices ["q-75977/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-75977/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-75977/selection/38861295b3aa8ed9988b03b0db770a1218cf647dc8d71f5fd60d72459c23a902" "q-75977/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-75977/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75977" :question/id #uuid "a9e03866-0890-54d2-8dd7-4c93154913fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-75977" :question/problem "The matrix $H$ is given below. Let ${h}_{1}$, ${h}_{2}$,  ${h}_{3}$ and ${h}_{4}$ be the respective columns of $H.$\nDetermine if $B=\\text{{}{h}_{1},{h}_{2}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(H).$ \nIf that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${h}_{4}={x}_{1}{h}_{1}+{x}_{2}{h}_{2}.$ \n\n$$\nH=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 12 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $H$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}H & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 12 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(H)$ is ${{h}_{1},{h}_{2},{h}_{3}}.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that $B={{h}_{1},{h}_{2}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(H).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-75977/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3bf9ea3-d57f-53f6-aa3c-eddffe1a8cfa